Dear Dr. M. Samir Gopalan,

I hope this message finds you well.

My name is Garima Jain, and I represent Umbrella by OkayLegal.ai =E2=80=94 a =
legal AI platform built in India to make legal clarity accessible to everyone=
, from citizens seeking their first understanding of a legal problem to advoc=
ates and law students preparing for practice.

We are reaching out to Silver Oak University, Ahmedabad, because we believe y=
our law students are exactly the audience that will shape the next generation=
 of the legal profession in Gujarat and across India. Your School of Law's co=
mmitment to value-based legal education and social transformation aligns clos=
ely with our mission: Justice served to everyone.

We would like to propose a guest talk (45=E2=80=9360 minutes) on:

"Justice for Everyone: How AI Is Reshaping Law in Gujarat and India"

The session would cover:
=E2=80=A2 Why access to justice remains India's biggest legal challenge =E2=
=80=94 and what Gujarat's legal ecosystem can do about it
=E2=80=A2 How AI is transforming legal research, drafting, and issue analysis=
 =E2=80=94 responsibly and with real citations
=E2=80=A2 What this means for law students entering practice in 2026 and beyo=
nd
=E2=80=A2 A live walkthrough of India-specific legal AI tools (court drafts, =
section finder, citation-backed research)

There is no cost to the university. We are mission-driven =E2=80=94 and we se=
e this as an investment in the students who will carry that mission forward.

We have attached a two-page brief about Umbrella and visuals for a potential =
moot court partnership we would love to explore after the guest session (the =
Umbrella Moot Court Challenge @ Silver Oak).

Would you =E2=80=94 or Ms. Nancy Jain, Associate Dean (Law) =E2=80=94 be open=
 to a short call this week or next to discuss dates and logistics?

Warm regards,

Garima Jain
